From 6e97969cfa142ac5ebbb1e312a2ff5a75e308e23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pierre Kisters <pierrekisters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:06:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(java): GHIDRA_MCP_FILE_ROOT takes several roots

The variable took one directory, so a server that must read from two
places (an upload directory and a scratch directory that another tool
writes into) had to widen the root to a common parent or drop it.

It now takes a list separated by the platform path separator (":" on
Linux and macOS, ";" on Windows). A path must fall under one entry,
compared as whole path components after canonicalization, so /workshop
is not under /work. One directory behaves as before; blank entries are
ignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
