 Changes on `dev` after 7.0.0.
 
+### Changed — `GHIDRA_MCP_FILE_ROOT` accepts several roots
+
+The variable took one directory, so a server that must read from two places (an upload
+directory and a scratch directory a tool writes into) had to widen the root to a common parent
+or drop it. It now takes a list separated by the platform path separator (`:` on Linux and
+macOS, `;` on Windows); a path must fall under one entry, compared as whole path components
+after canonicalization (`/workshop` is not under `/work`). A single directory behaves as
+before, and blank entries are ignored.
+
